# Threading & Data Flow

```
WorldReaderLoop ──► WorldSnapshot ──┐
                                    ├──► RadarApp.Tick ──► RenderContext ──► ImGuiRadarOverlay
Main loop (Tick)  ──► LiveFrame  ───┘
```

## Rules

- **One writer per mutable store** per thread; publish snapshots for readers.
- Use `_commandQueue` (or equivalent) to marshal UI/API actions onto the main tick thread.
- Lock only for small shared fields (e.g. overlay bounds); never hold locks across memory reads.
- `volatile` / interlocked for shutdown flags and published context pointers.

## Cadence separation

| Thread | Rate | Work |
|--------|------|------|
| Main | `FpsCap` | Hotkeys, live player, map lock, publish render ctx |
| World | `WorldRefreshHz` | Entity walk, terrain, nav replan inputs |
| ImGui | VSync / overlay | Draw only |

## Zone transitions

On `AreaInstance` change: invalidate entity caches, rebuild terrain bitmap, reset loot/atlas session state, clear stale paths. Don't carry pointers across zones.

## Shutdown

`RequestShutdown()` → drain loops; dispose `MemoryReader`/`ProcessHandle` via `using`; join background threads before exit.
